  "summary": "Three studies directly apply federated learning (or its functional equivalent—decentralised model updates aggregated on a server) to customer churn prediction. Brennan et al. [D0023] use federated learning on subscription logs from the GEFCom dataset, reporting an AUROC of 0.905. Okafor et al. [D0021] frame the same problem as privacy-preserving training across institutions without pooling data, using subscription logs from the MIMIC-IV dataset and reporting an F1 of 0.711. Iyer et al. [D0022] apply decentralised model updates aggregated on a server to subscription logs from the SentinelYield-2 dataset, reporting a MAPE of 0.8. A fourth study, Lindqvist et al. [D0024], also uses decentralised aggregation for anticipating subscriber cancellations on the GEFCom dataset, achieving an accuracy of 0.704. For context, Zhou et al. [D0027] address customer churn prediction with Bayesian hierarchical models (not federated learning) on the SentinelYield-2 dataset, reporting a MAPE of 0.705, providing a non-federated baseline on the same domain.",
